q BT 65.20 771.39 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (She raised the boss's son for twelve years. Then she learned who his real father was.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 741.91 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.345 Tw (Grace O'Connell was twenty-six when she answered an advertisement for a nanny in a house) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 721.50 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.417 Tw (she could not afford to look at. The house stood behind iron gates on a hill outside the city, and) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 701.09 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.790 Tw (the man who interviewed her was Salvatore Benedetti, a crime boss with a soft voice and eyes) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 680.68 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (that never blinked.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 651.20 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.957 Tw (The child was two years old. His name was Dominic. His mother had died in childbirth, or so) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 630.79 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.228 Tw (the house said, and his father needed someone to raise him properly. Grace took the job because) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 610.38 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (she needed the money, and she stayed because of the boy.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 580.90 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.014 Tw (She taught him to read. She taught him to ride a bicycle. She sat with him through fevers and) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 560.49 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.455 Tw (nightmares, and she told him stories to chase the dark away. Dominic grew up tall and kind,) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 540.09 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.008 Tw (with his mother's dark hair and a laugh that filled the house. He called her Gracie. She loved him) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 519.68 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.165 Tw (like her own son, and she told herself that was enough, that a nanny's love was a small and quiet) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 499.27 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (thing, and that small and quiet things were safe.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 469.79 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.814 Tw (It was not safe. Nothing in that house was safe. Grace had known it from the first week, when) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 449.38 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.078 Tw (she found a gun in a drawer she was told never to open, and a photograph in a book she was told) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 428.97 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (never to read.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 399.49 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.780 Tw (The photograph showed two young men, arms around each other's shoulders, laughing. One of) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 379.08 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 2.452 Tw (them was Salvatore Benedetti. The other was a man Grace knew better than anyone alive,) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 358.67 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (because she had grown up sharing a bedroom with him. Her brother, Anthony Russo.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 329.19 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.196 Tw (Anthony had died twelve years ago. The family said it was a car accident. Grace had buried him) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 308.78 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 3.227 Tw (herself, and she had never believed the story, not for a single day. Now, looking at the) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 288.37 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.042 Tw (photograph, she understood why. The two men in the picture had been best friends once. And) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 267.96 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.901 Tw (then something had happened between them, something that ended with one of them dead and) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 247.55 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (the other one rich.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 218.07 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.625 Tw (Grace kept the photograph. She put it back in the book, exactly where she found it, and she) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 197.66 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.251 Tw (never said a word. She watched Dominic grow, and she watched his face change, and she began) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 177.25 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.061 Tw (to see it: the shape of his jaw, the color of his eyes, the way he laughed. He did not look like) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 156.84 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (Salvatore Benedetti at all.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 127.36 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (He looked like Anthony Russo.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 97.88 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.431 Tw (For twelve years, Grace carried the question like a stone in her pocket. She told herself she was) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 77.47 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.036 Tw (imagining it. She told herself that grief makes ghosts out of ordinary faces. She told herself to be) Tj ET Q
